# ============================================================================
# THE FORM SETTINGS — what the contact form needs before it can send email.
#
# This file is an example. It holds no real values and it is safe to share.
# The real values are typed into two places and nowhere else:
#
#   the live site      at Netlify, where the site is hosted: Site
#                      configuration > Environment variables
#   this computer      in a file next to this one called .env.local, which
#                      git is told to ignore, so it is never shared
#
# Never paste a real key into this file, into a chat, or into anything that
# is shared. A key that has been shared is not reused: a new one is made at
# resend.com and the old one is left behind.
#
# Three settings. If any of the three is missing or empty, the live site
# refuses the form and tells the visitor plainly that it could not reach
# us, rather than saying thank you for a message that went nowhere.
#
# SO A LIVE BUILD STOPS WITHOUT THEM (5 October 2026). Before every build,
# scripts/check-form-env.mjs looks for all three; on Netlify's production
# build it fails the deploy if any is missing, and the live site stays on
# the last deploy that passed. Give the three a scope that includes Builds
# as well as Functions, or the check cannot see them. To publish with the
# form off on purpose, set ALLOW_FORM_OFF=1 in Netlify as well: the build
# then passes with a warning. Previews and this computer are never stopped.
# ============================================================================

# 1. THE KEY that lets the site send email through Resend (resend.com).
#    Where it comes from: Fadi creates a NEW key in his Resend account and
#    enters it himself. The old key is never reused.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# 2. WHERE ENQUIRIES GO. Every message from the contact form is emailed to
#    this address.
CONTACT_TO=a.hakim@recalibre.cloud

# 3. WHO THE EMAIL COMES FROM. An address on recalibre.cloud, written as
#    "Recalibre <name@recalibre.cloud>", with the < and > and without the
#    quotation marks.
#    The address is Fadi's, given on 25 September 2026. It sends only once
#    recalibre.cloud is verified with Resend.
#    Until it is set, the live site keeps the form off (Fadi's decision of
#    25 September 2026): the visitor is told the message could not be sent.
#    On this computer only, an empty value falls back to Resend's test
#    sender (onboarding@resend.dev), which only delivers to the owner of the
#    Resend account.
CONTACT_FROM=Recalibre <a.hakim@recalibre.cloud>

# Not a setting to enter: BUILD_YEAR, the year after the © in the menu and
# in the footer.
# The site writes it itself when it is built.
